# Codex PLAN review — P9A TweakSpec schema (disclaude). See "## PR P9A" in disclaude.md.

Tweaks today are an untyped AppSpec.tweaks dict + a stringly app_set_tweak. P9A adds the typed DEFINITION layer:
TweakEditor(str,Enum: text/color/int/float/boolean/enum/palette/null), TweakField (key/label/editor + per-editor
constraints: enum options, palette 2-5 colors, numeric min/max/step, affects-paths, controls_behavior), TweakSpec
(unique-keyed registry + validate_value per editor). A model_validator enforces enum-needs-options, palette-2..5,
numeric-needs-min/max/step (min<=max, step>0), and the JUSTIFICATION rule (a TEXT/COLOR tweak must control
behavior or >=2 fields, else it's ordinary editable content and rejected). Pure value objects; IO/tool/UI deferred
to P9B/C/D.

Judge: (a) is the TweakField/TweakEditor/TweakSpec shape right, and are the per-editor constraints complete/correct
(esp. numeric step-alignment, color hex validation, palette bounds)? (b) is the JUSTIFICATION rule (TEXT/COLOR
needs controls_behavior or affects>=2) the right encoding of "ordinary copy/color shouldn't be a tweak", or too
strict/loose — should affects be validated against a real AppSpec path namespace (deferred?) ? (c) should
validate_value COERCE (e.g. "true"->True, "3"->3) given the stringly legacy app_set_tweak, or strictly type-check?
(d) is separating the tweak DEFINITION (TweakSpec) from the VALUES (AppSpec.tweaks dict) the right model, and how
should they reconcile in P9B/C? (e) scope. Return APPROVE|REVISE|BLOCKED + REASONS + REQUIRED_REVISIONS.
